  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria Reduction Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Uganda):  The Malaria Reduction Activity (MRA) strengthens the capacity of the Ministry of Health&apos;s National Malaria Control Division and District Health Management Teams through a package of high-impact malaria interventions focused on community prevention and case management in high burden areas. These include distributing and promoting use of long-lasting insecticide treated nets during antenatal care, prevention of malaria during pregnancy, strengthening of diagnostics and treatment of malaria, social and behavior change, capacity strengthening, surveillance, operational research (for the Therapeutic Efficacy Test), and reporting. These aim to decrease malaria morbidity and mortality in 53 target districts in Busoga, Karamoja, West Nile, Lango, and Acholi. The Activity will protect approximately 13 million people from the effects of malaria.MRA will prevent gender-based violence and address the impact of gender-based violence. It will fund specific activities to reduce climate risks including support to Community Health Extension Workers (CHEWS) and Village Health Teams (VHTs) to provide integrated Community Case Management (iCCM) of malaria in target districts, some of which are flood-prone and likely to face health service delivery disruptions during floods and other natural disasters associated with climate change. MRA will provide funding to CHEWS and VHTs to conduct home to home visits and through interpersonal communication with household members, encourage removal of mosquito vector breeding grounds such as stagnant water and overall encourage proper household sanitation. MRA will include disaster preparedness, sanitation, and social behavior change activities aimed at reducing or mitigating climate risks to health in their annual work plans...</narrative>
  </description>
